1
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,680
[A fire three years ago]

2
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,480
[took everything from me.]

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,280
[My husband,]

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:16,760
[my child,]

5
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,200
[Xiaoyu,]

6
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,960
[and the innocent, happy version of me.]

7
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:23,680
[They all died in that explosion.]

8
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,120
[Consumed by hatred,]

9
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,240
[I changed my appearance.]

10
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,600
[I was certain that Lin Jiming, the heir to the Lin Group,]

11
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,720
[was the real culprit behind it all.]

12
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,960
[I approached him]

13
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:43,040
[to reveal the truth]

14
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,040
[and make him pay.]

15
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,520
[I warned myself not to fall for him.]

16
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,720
[But his sincerity,]

17
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:53,800
[tenderness,]

18
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,360
[innocence,]

19
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,400
[and subtle favor]

20
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:06,000
[still messed with my heart.]

21
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,720
[Until the car accident,]

22
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:15,080
[the moment he risked his life to save mine,]

23
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,040
[I was completely torn.]

24
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:21,480
[He was my sworn enemy,]

25
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,120
[but also the one who stole my heart.]

26
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:26,560
[I finally realized]

27
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,040
[that the hardest battle to overcome]

28
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:31,600
[was never about revenge,]

29
00:01:32,840 --> 00:01:33,720
[but]

30
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:35,440
[him.]

31
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:03,960
Mr. Lin,

32
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,680
this way.

33
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,320
He's here.

34
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,960
Here's the schedule for tonight's banquet.

35
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,880
This is the dance I learned just for you.

36
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,360
Lin Jiming,

37
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:33,840
watch carefully.

38
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,640
What's the biggest fear in a first impression?

39
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,400
It's mediocrity.

40
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:47,200
The key is to show your sexual tension

41
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:49,000
and uniqueness.

42
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:51,440
Only by standing out

43
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,920
can you become the target of attention.

44
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:00,360
Do you remember what the S in S club means?

45
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:02,640
Sexy.

46
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,120
Social.

47
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:05,720
Secret.

48
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,480
Eyes should be soft.

49
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,360
Posture should be firm.

50
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:13,680
Smile is a weapon.

51
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,040
Not an expression.

52
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:18,800
Not hold.

53
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,640
But pick.

54
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:20,760
Don't spill the wine.

55
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,000
Don't hide your smile.

56
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,440
Grace is not an act,

57
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:25,560
but a calculation.

58
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,320
Dancing is an excuse.

59
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,160
Touching is the purpose.

60
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,320
You have to make him feel

61
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:34,040
that you are guiding him,

62
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,120
not

63
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,480
he is controlling you.

64
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,560
Breathe lightly.

65
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,920
Use your eyes.

66
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,320
You are not dancing,

67
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,840
you are casting a net.

68
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:44,560
Others think you are the protagonist,

69
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,440
but they don't know

70
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,440
you are the real director.

71
00:03:59,320 --> 00:04:00,440
Next,

72
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,560
it's your turn.

73
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:05,880
Mr. Wen is here.

74
00:04:05,880 --> 00:04:07,720
Mr. Wen.

75
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:08,560
Nice to meet you, Mr. Wen.

76
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:31,920
Thank you all

77
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:34,000
for attending our Lin Group's charity gala.

78
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:35,240
I'd like to take this opportunity

79
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:37,200
to announce two things.

80
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:38,320
First,

81
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:40,120
I will gradually hand over the Lin Group

82
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,520
to my son,

83
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:42,840
Lin Jiming.

84
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:44,600
Secondly,

85
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,600
I'd like to introduce

86
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,360
Liu Yaruo,

87
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:53,960
the sister of our executive director,

88
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,200
Liu Yaping.

89
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,240
She and Jiming

90
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,800
will soon get engaged.

91
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,000
On the day

92
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,080
they get married,

93
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:02,280
Jiming will take full control

94
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,320
of the Lin Group.

95
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:18,840
Tian,

96
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,280
you look gorgeous today.

97
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,280
Many bosses asked me who you are.

98
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:23,520
Let's go.

99
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,400
Ms. Wei said

100
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,400
we should greet Mr. Zhang and Mr. Wang.

101
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:26,960
Okay.

102
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,280
Alright,

103
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:32,200
don't be so stiff.

104
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,400
If you want to see him,

105
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,400
just go ahead.

106
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,520
Alright.

107
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:41,680
Miss Liu

108
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:45,800
Jiming

109
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:47,240
What are you thinking about?

110
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:50,800
Nothing.

111
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:52,640
Actually, I didn't expect

112
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,160
Auntie Wen would suddenly

113
00:05:54,160 --> 00:05:55,640
announce us in public.

114
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:56,640
I didn't agree.

115
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,320
Look at Yaru and Jiming.

116
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,520
What a perfect match.

117
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:00,280
Yaping

118
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,280
From now on,

119
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:02,760
we are family.

120
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:04,960
Thank you, Mr. Wen,

121
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,360
for the opportunities you gave me.

122
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:08,000
I wish our Lin Group

123
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,360
can be listed as soon as possible.

124
00:06:10,320 --> 00:06:10,840
Yaping

125
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,440
will always be your soldier.

126
00:06:13,600 --> 00:06:14,400
Good.

127
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,680
Thank you.

128
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,040
Was it because I didn't discuss it with you in advance

129
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,200
that you're upset?

130
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,160
Did you discuss with me

131
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,640
about me being your girlfriend?

132
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:23,840
You...

133
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,280
Pretty,

134
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:43,800
don't rush to leave.

135
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,200
You've got the moves,

136
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,960
now let's drink up!

137
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:47,600
Come on.

138
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,800
Have another drink with me.

139
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,440
Mr. Wang,

140
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,040
please behave yourself.

141
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:53,680
Let go.

142
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,360
Don't act all high and mighty.

143
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:56,920
You dancers are all the same.

144
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:57,640
Who's that?

145
00:06:59,040 --> 00:06:59,480
Lin...

146
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:00,400
Mr. Lin.

147
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,040
Get lost.

148
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:04,880
Mr. Lin,

149
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,320
what do you mean?

150
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,920
I don't want to repeat myself.

151
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:08,960
Fine.

152
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:10,320
I'll leave.

153
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,920
You look tired.

154
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,480
Alcohol can ease sorrow,

155
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,040
but it can also cause trouble.

156
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,120
You'd better drink less.

157
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:03,440
The dance you just performed

158
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:04,200
was really good.

159
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:09,960
Don't put on airs.

160
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:10,760
Dancers like you

161
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:11,240
are all...

162
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:11,840
Who's there?

163
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:14,400
Alcohol can drown sorrows,

164
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:15,760
but it can also lead to trouble.

165
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,240
Better to drink less.

166
00:08:22,720 --> 00:08:23,520
Thank you for your hard work today.

167
00:08:23,520 --> 00:08:24,520
Thank you.

168
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:25,200
Thanks.

169
00:08:28,320 --> 00:08:29,320
Bait is set,

170
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:31,120
waiting for you to take the hook.

171
00:08:34,240 --> 00:08:35,520
Your idea was brilliant.

172
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:37,160
Two women dancing

173
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:38,480
is indeed more dynamic

174
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:39,720
and more enchanting.

175
00:08:40,120 --> 00:08:40,960
I heard

176
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:42,840
the entire audience was in awe.

177
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,240
It's all thanks to your excellent coaching.

178
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:45,840
Well,

179
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:47,640
didn't you used to

180
00:08:47,920 --> 00:08:49,760
refuse to attend these events?

181
00:08:51,040 --> 00:08:52,040
Didn't you say

182
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,280
high-end events are our hunting grounds?

183
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,040
I'm not ready yet,

184
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,320
how dare I go into battle?

185
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,080
You sure know how to talk.

186
00:09:01,480 --> 00:09:01,960
By the way,

187
00:09:02,480 --> 00:09:03,040
Wei,

188
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:05,560
do you have a membership to the Beagle Club?

189
00:09:05,760 --> 00:09:06,280
What?

190
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,720
You want to go there?

191
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:08,800
I heard

192
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:10,680
that club is really good,

193
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,400
so

194
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,360
I want to check it out.

195
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:13,160
Alright,

196
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,200
use my membership.

197
00:09:40,960 --> 00:09:41,920
Isn't it boring

198
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:44,520
to play alone?

199
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:51,760
It's you.

200
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,280
What are you doing here?

201
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,040
Maybe

202
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,320
I'm here to meet you.

203
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,240
In that case,

204
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:05,560
let's have a game.

205
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,520
Okay.

206
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:08,120
If you win, it's up to you.

207
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:09,800
If I win,

208
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:11,160
you have to answer a question.

209
00:10:13,680 --> 00:10:14,440
Ladies first.

210
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,360
This is how you play.

211
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,000
I lost.

212
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,200
My question is,

213
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:42,240
a life arranged by others

214
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,000
must be exhausting, right?

215
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,800
Who are you exactly?

216
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:57,800
Someone who can help you.

217
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,360
What do you know?

218
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,840
I understand your discontent.

219
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,040
You're capable,

220
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,160
but trapped in marriage.

221
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:19,840
You work

222
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,600
hard on your own,

223
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:24,200
yet people point fingers and say

224
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,160
it's all because of your parents.

225
00:12:27,880 --> 00:12:29,000
You know me well.

226
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,600
You want to resist,

227
00:12:30,880 --> 00:12:32,360
but you can't, right?

228
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:39,480
Actually, life is like snooker.

229
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,440
Sometimes,

230
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:42,760
mistakes

231
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,400
are the best offense.

232
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:02,920
You're drunk.

233
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:05,320
How about we

234
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,760
go somewhere else to sober up?

235
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:11,800
You know,

236
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:13,240
some people

237
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,680
are born to live in the fire.

238
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:18,320
Either they are burnt to ashes,

239
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:21,160
or they temper themselves into a sword.

240
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,440
Guess

241
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,400
which one I am.

242
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,760
Your heart is beating so fast.

243
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,680
Is it because of desire,

244
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:31,440
or

245
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:33,480
because you smell a familiar scent?

246
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:35,200
Shh.

247
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:36,960
Don't answer so quickly.

248
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:39,560
Tonight,

249
00:13:41,120 --> 00:13:42,120
I'll let you win.

250
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:57,360
Good night,

251
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,000
Mr. Heir.

252
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:00,800
I hope your dreams

253
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,600
are cleaner than mine.
